    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Drake Baldwin** (69.51) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14), our top-ranked plays. Both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Dobnak, whose 4.61 xERA provides a soft landing for our leadoff-hitting pair. **Henry Bolte** also warrants attention; despite the right-on-right matchup against Lambert, his 59.84 score is buoyed by a 10% park factor boost and his prime leadoff positioning. While **Kyle Tucker** (53.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (51.39) face stiffer competition against Pivetta and Glasnow respectively, their high-floor profiles remain essential to our daily offensive production, even with the SP skill headwinds pulling their scores toward the marginal range.\n\nThe benching of **Wade Meckler** (42.97) was the most difficult personnel decision of the morning. While he offered decent utility potential, his score was suppressed by a poor park factor and a difficult matchup against Woo, ultimately forcing him to the bench in favor of our higher-efficiency starts. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Heliot Ramos** (47.69) and **Brayan Rocchio** (45.80); both face pitchers with xERAs below 4.00, and **Brayan Rocchio** specifically deals with a \"wind in\" scenario that adds a layer of volatility to his floor. As we navigate this late-season push, we remain wary of the heavy workload placed on our core, while we continue to monitor the status of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg** to ensure our roster depth\u2014including prospects like **Coby Mayo**, **Tommy White**, and **Franklin Arias**\u2014is ready to plug any unexpected gaps.",
